From: FunnyPlaying RetroPixel Pocket port
Subject: [PATCH] usb: dwc2: preserve RPPocket stock timeout calibration

The RPPocket stock kernel leaves GUSBCFG.TOUTCAL at its reset value while
bringing up the internal RTL8188EUS on the DWC2 OTG controller. Mainline sets
TOUTCAL(7), after which this board never observes the internal USB device.

Keep the stock register behavior only on the RPPocket. This quirk has been
validated across cold boot and repeated DWC2 unload/reload suspend cycles.

---
 drivers/usb/dwc2/hcd.c | 11 ++++++++---
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/usb/dwc2/hcd.c b/drivers/usb/dwc2/hcd.c
--- a/drivers/usb/dwc2/hcd.c
+++ b/drivers/usb/dwc2/hcd.c
@@ -18,6 +18,7 @@
 #include <linux/usb.h>
 
 #include <linux/usb/hcd.h>
+#include <linux/of.h>
 #include <linux/usb/ch11.h>
 #include <linux/usb/of.h>
 
@@ -2144,10 +2145,14 @@ static void dwc2_core_host_init(struct dwc2_hsotg *hsotg)
 	 * introduced by the PHY. This can be required, because the delay
 	 * introduced by the PHY in generating the linestate condition
 	 * can vary from one PHY to another.
+	 *
+	 * The RPPocket stock firmware leaves TOUTCAL at its reset value.
 	 */
-	usbcfg = dwc2_readl(hsotg, GUSBCFG);
-	usbcfg |= GUSBCFG_TOUTCAL(7);
-	dwc2_writel(hsotg, usbcfg, GUSBCFG);
+	if (!of_machine_is_compatible("funnyplaying,rppocket")) {
+		usbcfg = dwc2_readl(hsotg, GUSBCFG);
+		usbcfg |= GUSBCFG_TOUTCAL(7);
+		dwc2_writel(hsotg, usbcfg, GUSBCFG);
+	}
 
 	/* Restart the Phy Clock */
 	dwc2_writel(hsotg, 0, PCGCTL);
